```

But wait — if machineLogins is undefined (defensive), `{authorLogins: undefined}` → allow = null (since Array.isArray(undefined) false) → unfiltered. Hmm, but the doctrine says readers ALWAYS pass an allowlist. If callers always pass an array (possibly empty), then unconfigured → [] → trust nothing → guards inert → legacy. OK.

