}
```

Now the memo caches the raw list (keyed by prNumber only), and parsing happens per call with the allowlist. Fail-open: broken read → [] cached → parses to []. 

But wait — memoized value semantics change from "records" to "raw list". The memo is internal (kind prVerdicts), no external consumer reads it as records? ioCache is module-private; only used via these functions. But there was a test 'verdictRecords memoizes per tick' expecting 1 fetch for 3 reads — still holds.

Hmm, one concern: caching raw comment bodies vs parsed records — memory fine.

Also `parseVerdictRecords` outside try/catch — pure function, no throw. OK.

