Both sites are inside the same rule-item loop within `processRuleLocally` where `effectiveConfig` is in scope. I'll compute the verdict allowlist once per item right where needed. To keep it DRY, compute at each call site via a small helper. Is there an existing helper in smAgent for "machine logins for verdict"? No. I'll add a tiny helper near readVerdictRecords:

```js
// The gh-728 machine-author allowlist for verdict-record parsing (gh-828
// review round 2) — resolved from the same knob chain as every other
// machine-keyed guard; unconfigured → [] (trust nothing).
function verdictMachineLogins(effectiveConfig) {
    return machineAuthorModule.machineAuthorLogins(
        machineAuthorModule.resolveMachineAuthor(RUN_JOB_PARAMS, effectiveConfig));
}
```

Then call sites pass `verdictMachineLogins(effectiveConfig)`.

